{"agent": "researcher", "description": "Analyze calc.py tax logic", "background": true, "prompt": "Purpose: The user wants a plan to unify tax calculation across a small Python repo. This package tells us what calc.py does and how it handles tax, if at all.

Scope: Repo at /private/tmp/oceval/work/c4-subagents-control. Read calc.py (find it with glob if it isn't at the root). Report every function: its signature and what it does. Pay special attention to anything about tax: tax rates, constants, rounding, and helper functions. Also note any imports of calc.py from other files, using grep. READ-ONLY: do not edit, create or delete any file.

Done: Return a concise report with (1) the file path, (2) a list of functions/constants with one-line descriptions and line numbers, (3) the exact tax-related code quoted with line numbers, or an explicit "no tax logic", (4) who imports calc.py. Cite file:line for every claim."}

{"agent": "researcher", "description": "Analyze price.py and invoice.py tax", "background": true, "prompt": "Purpose: The user wants a plan to unify tax calculation across a small Python repo. This package tells us what price.py and invoice.py do and how each one computes tax, so we can find duplication.

Scope: Repo at /private/tmp/oceval/work/c4-subagents-control. Read price.py and invoice.py (find them with glob if they aren't at the root). For each file, report every function: its signature and what it does. Pay special attention to tax: rate values (hard-coded literals or constants), formulas, rounding, and whether either file imports from the other or from calc.py. List any tests that cover them (grep for test files). READ-ONLY: do not edit, create or delete any file.

Done: Return a concise report with (1) file paths, (2) the functions in each file with one-line descriptions and line numbers, (3) the exact tax-related code from each file quoted with line numbers, (4) the differences between the two tax implementations (rate, formula, rounding), (5) imports and related tests. Cite file:line for every claim."}
